=== COMPILER BLOCKER FOUND + WORKED AROUND (pre-existing, confirmed at HEAD) ===
The whole-app iOS/macOS build was blocked BEFORE this run by a Swift 6.3.2
swift-frontend IRGen crash (report_fatal_error/abort), NOT a type error:
    "While evaluating request IRGenRequest(IR Generation for file
     .../TeslaSync/feature-views/AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift)"
    "While emitting IR SIL function @$sSbScA_pSgIeAghyg_SbIeAghn_TR"
The mangled thunk is the reabstraction of a `@MainActor (Bool) -> Void` closure
(the `(any Actor)?` isolation in the name) into SwiftUI `Binding`'s non-isolated
setter — `AppearanceToggleRow`'s `Toggle("", isOn: Binding(get:set: onChange))`.
PROVEN PRE-EXISTING: stashed ALL of this run's changes, regenerated, and rebuilt
clean HEAD → identical crash, ** BUILD FAILED ** (same file, same thunk). It is
owned by the P4 `AppearanceSettings` surface (commit 0dd623aa3), not P9-0002, and
is the documented "pre-existing parallel-merge full-app blocker" class from
apps/macos-pending-verifications.md.
WORKAROUND (1 spot, behaviour-preserving): wrap the Toggle setter so user code
performs the isolation hop instead of the crashing compiler-emitted thunk:
    set: { value in MainActor.assumeIsolated { onChange(value) } }
SwiftUI always calls Binding setters on the main actor, so assumeIsolated is safe.
Blast radius measured: the single change let the WHOLE app build proceed past every
sibling file to compile this run's Sources/Dev — i.e. it was one spot, not whack-a-
mole. This unblocks the shared iOS build for every Apple artifact.

